PURPOSE

A37 showed that bounded lineage memory is real
but does not materially break
the persistent FAMILY-5 oscillatory attractor.

A post-closure diagnostic localized that attractor.

Balanced periodic forcing:

1/1;
2/2;
3/3;
4/4

almost never produced FAMILY-5 oscillation.

The persistent failures are concentrated in:

6/2;
inverted 2/6;
5/3;
inverted 3/5.

Those four contexts have
a strong long-run candidate advantage,
but contain repeated short stale-favoring counter-pulses.

Therefore the current failure is not:

inability to represent equal ambiguity.

It is:

population-wide overreaction
to short adverse bursts
inside a longer-run coherent signal.

A38 tests whether
different cells should respond
on different temporal timescales.

No lineage-memory mechanism from A37 is carried forward.

A37 answered that question negatively.

A38 returns to the full A36 NICHE organism
and changes one mechanism only:

the temporal integration used
by committed cells
when deciding whether local opposition
is strong enough to force defection.

