THE ONLY NEW MECHANISM — LOCAL TEMPORAL OPPOSITION TRACE

Every cell maintains two local traces:

O_C(i,t):

temporally integrated local S opposition
relevant to staying C.

O_S(i,t):

temporally integrated local C opposition
relevant to staying S.

At every epoch,
before committed-state defection decisions:

L_S(i,t)
=
current local S-emitter density
within the frozen A30 radius 12.

L_C(i,t)
=
current local C-emitter density.

For a cell with memory coefficient rho:

O_C(i,t)
=
rho * O_C(i,t-1)
+
(1-rho) * L_S(i,t).

O_S symmetrically.

Initial traces:

0.

Traces update for every cell
regardless of current phenotype.

Thus newly committed cells
already carry their own recent
local environmental history.

The traces are local dynamical state.

They are not:

confidence;
probability of correctness;
or a global statistic.

DEFECTION LAW

The A30 Hill persistence law remains:

p_stay
=
