A38_TEMPORAL_DIVERSITY_INFORMATION_GAIN

TRUE iff at least one MIXED arm:

reduces overall oscillation versus FAST;

breaks at least 25%
of FAST biased-periodic oscillators;

has lower biased-periodic oscillation
than both FAST and at least one
homogeneous slower arm;

retains reversal acquisition >= 0.80;

and retains >= 90% FAST service.

This explicitly distinguishes:

"slower is better"

from:

"mixed timescales are better."

